Keep the Touch Bar out of brightness 0.

Some MacBookPro17,1 Touch Bar panels flash white, often about once a second,
while their backlight is held at 0, which tiny-dfr uses after 60 s without
input and whenever the lid is closed
(https://github.com/AsahiLinux/tiny-dfr/issues/32). Stay at the dimmed level
(1) instead, and paint the bar black so it still looks off (black OLED pixels
are unlit, so the faint image doesn't age the panel). A closed lid matters
too: with lid-closed operation or a docked display, the laptop can run for
hours with the bar flashing unseen under the lid. Touches are ignored until
input or opening the lid wakes the bar, as tiny-dfr already does at
brightness 0.

